            "quote": "A10 Liveness does not close semantic truth. Liveness observes activity,\ninactivity, process state and interruption. It can support yield or a\nliveness interruption; it cannot by itself declare semantic failure,\nsemantic closure or requirement non-satisfaction (P6).",
            "section": "urn:a-c:project:8ae07eeca101a93be143e873f9d12ab43e316ef0359058c0c9fa71380880d2d5/source/build_tenants/a_c/representation/stdo-v3.0.5-rc.1/source/standards/ODD.md#ODD%2F11.%20Core%20law%2F11.5D%20Constructive%20evaluation%20and%20yield%20loop",
            "start_line": 1246
          }
        ],
        "statement": "Yield requires the same edge/attempt to remain lawful, admitted progress/waiting, replay-visible resume basis and control return without failure classification. It preserves the current edge for long-running, bounded or partially productive work and is not retry, block, timeout or a local CLI loop. Liveness alone cannot establish semantic failure, closure, requirement non-satisfaction or retry(defeated). It can support yield or interruption.",
        "uncertainty": ""
      },
