          {
            "end_line": 198,
            "path": "build_tenants/a_c/representation/stdo-v3.0.5-rc.1/source/plugins/spec/references/COORDINATED_HANDOFF.md",
            "quote": "## Evaluate The Return\n\nThe issuer checks activation identity, exact subject/basis, result variant,\nevidence scope and invalidators before relying on the return. It acquires\nonly the return projection its own frame permits; a link to a full artifact\ndoes not authorize reading it. A digest authenticates bytes, not their claims.\n\nReconcile an effect whose completion or end remains unknown before retry or\nany dependent action (`ACTIVATION` §3 Effects and §5). A timeout, missing\nmessage or lost context is not evidence that no effect occurred. Retain valid\nprogress; do not replay a step merely because its actor changed.\n\nApply the governing result/disposition relation and determine whether the\nexact candidate requires independent review. Issue `stdo-review` separately\nwhere required. Reviewer severity remains its technical assessment; the\ndecision owner assigns priority and boundary effect within its grant\n(`EXECUTIVE_BASELINE` §12 steps 4–7). Do not turn a closed result into implicit\nauthority to repair, accept, publish or start the next stage.\n\nA proposed next action is not an executable activation. Before calling it\nalready authorized or issuing it, bind the actual operation grant and the\nsettled subject/pass grouping required by that contract. If either is missing,\nreturn the proposal and exact unresolved binding; do not presume a Writer grant\nor combine unsettled passes. This checks the existing intake, not a new gate.\n\nFor an admitted sequence, each continuation uses the previous closed result\nand current bindings. Retain the boundaries the contract actually declares:\nneither a new human check-in at every pass nor review only at the end is a\nuniversal rule. Refresh affected bindings on material change, not every\nunchanged status observation (`ACTIVATION` §1 Roles and delegation; §7).",
            "section": "urn:a-c:project:8ae07eeca101a93be143e873f9d12ab43e316ef0359058c0c9fa71380880d2d5/source/build_tenants/a_c/representation/stdo-v3.0.5-rc.1/source/plugins/spec/references/COORDINATED_HANDOFF.md#Coordinated%20Skill%20Handoff%2FEvaluate%20The%20Return",
            "start_line": 169
          }
        ],
        "statement": "Acquire only the return projection allowed to the consumer; a full-artifact link is not a read grant. Reconcile unknown completion before retry or dependent action; timeout or lost message proves no absence of effects. Preserve valid progress across actors. Apply the actual disposition relation and separately activate required independent review; a closed return grants no repair, acceptance, publication or next stage. Bind the actual operation grant and settled subject/pass grouping before calling a next action already authorized. Refresh material changes; impose neither an extra human check-in every pass nor review-only-at-end as universal rules.",
        "uncertainty": ""
      },
